NAME
     usertests - the kernel's own tests

SYNOPSIS
     usertests [-q] [NAME...]

DESCRIPTION
     usertests runs the system-call tests against a running kernel:
     the file system, permissions, the clock, copy-on-write, lazy
     allocation, mmap, signals, threads and the terminal. It prints a
     line per test and ALL TESTS PASSED at the end.

OPTIONS
     -q       the quicker set
     NAME...  only these tests
